  "summary": "whalibmob@5.33.26: static keyword co-occurrence without traced installer-harm evidence",
  "details": "a static rule fired on keyword co-occurrence in lib/MediaService.js (fs + http/https + readFileSync + https.request), lib/Registration.js (repeated 'ping' tokens), lib/WebVersion.js (curl, https.get, ps), and lib/socks.js (curl, POST, hostname). No concrete attacker-controlled destination, credential path read, lifecycle-script execution, or install/import-time dropper is identified from the available evidence, and semantic tracing of the flagged files did not corroborate a specific exfiltration or RCE flow. The patterns are consistent with legitimate uses (HTTP client code, process utilities, SOCKS proxy helper, media handling) as well as with malicious ones; the keyword co-occurrence alone does not establish an attacker-benefit mechanism against the installer.",
